Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip-inno-usb2: refresh host state on line interrupt

A host can miss its disconnect-fall interrupt during enumeration.
The cached host_disconnect flag then stays true despite a connected hub.
The periodic worker suspends that PHY when it samples a zero line state.

On TSPI-4M, tracing captured this suspend at 125.917 seconds.
The fc880000 EHCI frame counter stopped immediately afterwards.

Use the enabled line-state interrupt to clear the stale disconnect flag.
Ignore line-state status when its interrupt is disabled.
This matches the Rockchip 6.1 BSP connection-state handling.

---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -1052,7 +1052,8 @@ static irqreturn_t rockchip_usb2phy_linestate_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	struct rockchip_usb2phy_port *rport = data;
 	struct rockchip_usb2phy *rphy = dev_get_drvdata(rport->phy->dev.parent);
 
-	if (!property_enabled(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->ls_det_st))
+	if (!property_enabled(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->ls_det_st) ||
+	    !property_enabled(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->ls_det_en))
 		return IRQ_NONE;
 
 	mutex_lock(&rport->mutex);
@@ -1061,6 +1062,10 @@ static irqreturn_t rockchip_usb2phy_linestate_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	property_enable(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->ls_det_en, false);
 	property_enable(rphy->grf, &rport->port_cfg->ls_det_clr, true);
 
+	if (rport->port_id == USB2PHY_PORT_HOST &&
+	    rport->port_cfg->disfall_en.offset)
+		rport->host_disconnect = false;
+
 	mutex_unlock(&rport->mutex);
 
 	/*
